er-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7467eff-3284-5ff8-926d-e47188223d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234908} :answer-field/id #uuid "75fbad98-0a41-5480-ba06-edccdf81f980" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235112}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "413988df-903b-557d-87b6-8594e3b605b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-167636" :question/problem "If $k(x)=g(x)-f(x),$ where $A=2$ and $B=3,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "We found that $A=2$ and $B=3$ in steps 3 and 4, respectively. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =g(x)-f(x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{x}-({x}^{3}+2x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the addition and power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{e}^{x}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =3{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58606740-b081-5671-ab93-5b28309b7d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}+2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58606740-b081-5671-ab93-5b28309b7d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}+2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234683} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0bd4a86-aed0-5919-98b7-ad23d53bddbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfc04756-ffae-5a03-8a05-d0ea5dfb5207" :question/math-academy-id "q-167694" :question/problem "For $x<1,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "For $x<1,$ we use the expression $f(x)={e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x,$ which is differentiable.\n\nUsing the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}+2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0884ad38-9d14-5f8e-b665-d8b35b5af237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269346} {:answer/id #uuid "0db0ac08-c4ce-5d3f-845f-d38358413506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269388} {:answer/id #uuid "2934301c-7684-5c1f-b910-d7819431eba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269640} {:answer/id #uuid "7789397b-7630-5bd8-9c80-42e72f128cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270328} {:answer/id #uuid "81639cc6-e903-5cd2-bc14-50bfc72b4d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7789397b-7630-5bd8-9c80-42e72f128cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270328} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c2979c-8072-5209-9ca0-20ccbaf77003" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271876}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2ffa4af-5dbe-569b-8d78-f233584a8913" :question/math-academy-id "q-140431" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2{e}^{x}+4{x}^{2}-3$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}+4{x}^{2}-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+0 \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}+8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(2{e}^{x}+8x)\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {e}^{1}+8\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2e+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272086 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1859eb59-5659-5101-b949-46d66d579831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269472} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0e81a7-1d07-50d3-b00e-dd0c50955d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+6e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269501} {:answer/id #uuid "2d71f9f8-72d8-5409-b4ca-0645cd6983b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+6e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269679} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ca486a-dc13-5bb9-932e-532847144371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270990} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a796d4-403d-5aad-82ff-004acd0b4a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5a796d4-403d-5aad-82ff-004acd0b4a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271012} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c8b5dd-9fdc-5213-98ff-f269c094b6e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271882}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "578adda7-12d4-5f1e-a8c7-f591ce6d42cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-140432" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{2}+2x+6{e}^{x}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+2x+6{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x+2+6{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(2x+2+6{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+2+6\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =2+6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "397833d7-9cc6-50ae-8de7-3a5674155a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282196} {:answer/id #uuid "8d66fe18-2e0a-548c-a20c-052aa8a29cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282914} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc41fd0-6fd9-5709-9af2-b2dd6b711472" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283503} {:answer/id #uuid "df2ebee4-e1b4-5f85-bbbc-9c810b46a256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283637} {:answer/id #uuid "fe32be51-d0ac-5644-92b4-204731798028" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df2ebee4-e1b4-5f85-bbbc-9c810b46a256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283637} :answer-field/id #uuid "34cf92cc-bcc5-56af-93bf-714a48258bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284027}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5816a349-a320-5d09-93fc-2ee07a9147af" :question/math-academy-id "q-17247" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-3(2x) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(2{e}^{x}-6x)\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =2{e}^{0}-6\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ad567a-37aa-5c67-8461-48b832a97b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282410} {:answer/id #uuid "84f495d5-d4be-5db4-8f35-da2bca8cfe2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282836} {:answer/id #uuid "9e412a36-003f-51b6-80db-13d3f13969a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283068} {:answer/id #uuid "a99e9fb3-9911-531b-94e1-18309a3f6530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283157} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bf7484-ada1-5d36-86d4-7dceaa4a2600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54ad567a-37aa-5c67-8461-48b832a97b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282410} :answer-field/id #uuid "114801c2-0284-5663-a95f-f2fe249472cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7bb16ef-b727-58e4-9164-1a907f3660c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-17255" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=11{e}^{x}+8{x}^{2}-12x-20$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{e}^{x}+8{x}^{2}-12x-20) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =11\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =11{e}^{x}+8(2x)-12(1)-0 \\\\  & =11{e}^{x}+16x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(11{e}^{x}+16x-12)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =11{e}^{0}+16\\cdot 0-12 \\\\  & =11\\cdot 1+0-12 \\\\  & =11-12 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b89210db-d5da-5a48-8355-741becb1873c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42+\\frac{2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296232} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f887ee-f564-4711-a252-4f52754bf8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42x^6+2e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b89210db-d5da-5a48-8355-741becb1873c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42+\\frac{2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296232} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca439fbc-124d-5dae-b8b3-a85cb6575e03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297054}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f66d07e-3ca1-595a-b1d7-b4c775329676" :question/math-academy-id "q-304035" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=6{x}^{7}+2{e}^{x}$, the exact value of the slope of the tangent line at $x=-1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{7}+2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =6(7{x}^{6})+2{e}^{x} \\\\  & =42{x}^{6}+2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & ={(42{x}^{6}+2{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =42(-1)^{6}+2{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =42\\cdot 1+\\frac{2}{e} \\\\  & =42+\\frac{2}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Polynomial"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096612 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096412 :question/id #uuid "16b1a91c-ae83-5e6b-a11d-bb9d78e4d218" :question/math-academy-id "e-3626" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=3 \\cdot 2^x$, find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tf'(x)      &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(3 \\cdot 2^x\\right) \\\n                            &= 3 \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(2^x\\right) \\\n                            &=  3 \\cdot 2^{x}\\ln(2) \\\n                            &=  3 \\ln(2) \\cdot 2^{x}.\n\t}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "14e68965-6c39-5947-ac05-eee99e685063" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d843f8b3-130e-58a5-9fbd-82ec568db2c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 5 \\cdot 2^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093921} {:answer/id #uuid "014e0413-2e84-53f7-b45a-ddf3de5c66ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = \\frac{5 \\cdot 2^{x}}{\\ln 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093922} {:answer/id #uuid "59ffeb59-c600-576e-b386-4238d5be4435" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = \\frac{5\\ln 2}{2^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093923} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7bb843-7ffc-5cee-ae0d-c06b53bc9748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 5\\ln 2 \\cdot 2^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093924}] :answer-field/id #uuid "391923fc-8733-5f78-b82d-8361511793c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093920}] :question/id #uuid "991df192-1bbb-5ddd-b9f8-9c449c0a2bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-11732" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = 5 \\cdot 2^{x}$, find $f^{′}(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84fac42b-8598-507e-a597-b51cf44552e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 4^{x}\\ln 4 + 3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094904} {:answer/id #uuid "9f573042-c991-5b93-95cd-f442a342ef79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = \\ln 4 + 3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094905} {:answer/id #uuid "a83c0a13-5121-5e13-b635-203e453d1fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 4^{x} - \\ln 4 + 3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094906} {:answer/id #uuid "e39ac619-c915-5405-9fdf-5d74bfe05e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 4^{x}\\ln x + 3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094907} {:answer/id #uuid "71daaeac-c06c-5a66-a1ba-95951dbcd11e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{′}(x) = 4^{x} + 3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094908}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4b148928-ba92-5c24-b71d-675d583ec080" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094903}] :question/id #uuid "e0af69f1-1a58-5ac7-90e2-c2859723b842" :question/math-academy-id "q-1917" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = 4^{x} + 3e^{x}$, find $f^{′}(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3232bdcf-d781-5e59-bb5b-56c10f0d7fa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250976} {:answer/id #uuid "37865371-b061-54aa-9810-81e59d0b835b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6}^{x}-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251009} {:answer/id #uuid "3d09661f-ce26-5e19-a8b8-2ae50263662e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251060} {:answer/id #uuid "9007950f-ce55-5f0c-a1f6-d3963f0294f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6}^{x}-10x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251775} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf32e0c-8341-5060-b67e-c44870ab4cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d09661f-ce26-5e19-a8b8-2ae50263662e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251060} :answer-field/id #uuid "e849ca6e-9bda-5244-a669-0f22826facaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253210}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50678a5c-afcb-522f-98fb-80e9680afca6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11735" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =ln⁡6\\cdot {6}^{x}-5(2x)+6(1)-0 \\\\  & ={6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284697 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbb468a-9928-5c35-89ed-eaf197f78886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281954} {:answer/id #uuid "618693f7-594d-59ce-a534-76a8e9e2b379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡3+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282519} {:answer/id #uuid "888a6635-e022-5c1a-a6c7-78955c8928cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡3+5e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282867} {:answer/id #uuid "8957ae1d-f55e-532c-822e-e38dcfa2b32c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282874} {:answer/id #uuid "956605d2-ce2e-57d7-b286-ab43b24751bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "618693f7-594d-59ce-a534-76a8e9e2b379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡3+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282519} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7e9ba42-2c84-571b-94b9-4df571509ab4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284227}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e51c642-d912-5d35-8cf2-7c273fba130d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17388" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}+5{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}+5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}ln⁡3+5{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={({3}^{x}ln⁡3+5{e}^{x})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & ={3}^{0}ln⁡3+5{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\cdot ln⁡3+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =ln⁡3+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3554bc38-45ed-5174-b2e0-b7a82dde78d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}(8){8}^{x}+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3554bc38-45ed-5174-b2e0-b7a82dde78d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}(8){8}^{x}+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295565} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a6fdabb-ec35-5bee-8e6f-6b6e93c3ccd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296661}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4df22161-f9b7-5077-b623-7a70a19c609f" :question/math-academy-id "q-304038" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=3\\cdot {8}^{x}+12x+10$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {8}^{x}+12x+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {8}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({8}^{x})+12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =3(ln⁡(8){8}^{x})+12(1)+0 \\\\  & =3ln⁡(8){8}^{x}+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314919 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202a3876-df45-5f69-9dea-3b48cc477974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}(8){8}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312218} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad5377e-557d-4b02-81f5-eba612380c71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot8^{x}\\ln8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "202a3876-df45-5f69-9dea-3b48cc477974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}(8){8}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312218} :answer-field/id #uuid "5168e7a2-5958-57af-b48a-ff61e1073f47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314237}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca876738-9b8d-5832-85d7-2d09df78130a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340272" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=7-2\\cdot {8}^{x}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-2\\cdot {8}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\cdot {8}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({8}^{x}) \\\\  & =0-2(ln⁡(8){8}^{x}) \\\\  & =-2ln⁡(8){8}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40066746-e699-53ed-82fd-0f35f8e924c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(5)+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312491} {:answer/id #uuid "8688c450-e972-4ef8-abf7-296b751229f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5^{x}\\ln5-18x^2+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40066746-e699-53ed-82fd-0f35f8e924c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(5)+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312491} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4ba52fe-3ccd-59f7-bca4-208b03b18375" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314595}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2b3624c-f62d-5f81-b0de-c13d8e4bf17c" :question/math-academy-id "q-340280" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={5}^{x}-6{x}^{3}+4x-1$, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x}-6{x}^{3}+4x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x})-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-6(3{x}^{2})+4(1)-0 \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-18{x}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{x}-18{x}^{2}+4)|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{0}-18(0)^{2}+4 \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)\\cdot 1-0+4 \\\\  & =ln⁡(5)+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Exponential Function with a Base Other Than e"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096613 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096413 :question/id #uuid "6624681a-bb00-59db-8df9-4d5a3cd00434" :question/math-academy-id "e-3627" :question/problem "Given that $y=5\\ln x$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( \\ln x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}   & = \\left(5\\ln x\\right)'\\  \n                                                    & = 5 (\\ln x)'\\\n                                                    &=5\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}\\\n                                                    &= \\dfrac{5}{x}.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t  \n\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048932 :topic/math-academy-id 278 :topic/title "The Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "957a337d-5366-5ff2-837c-52484ac86768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094100} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a5634d-31a1-562b-a09a-feb05e88887c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094101} {:answer/id #uuid "4832dd38-53a9-5b87-8cd8-b896e7db9350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094102} {:answer/id #uuid "542026ef-81ef-58c0-a96c-df6b38bc70ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094103} {:answer/id #uuid "67a422d5-e423-5c10-8c25-5930bf5bc45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094104}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c7111e8a-6b0b-59ab-9d87-0933257a4569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094099}] :question/id #uuid "39f62811-3b9a-5225-ae53-715b926ed4a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11909" :question/problem "Given that $y = 7\\ln x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd19f85a-2650-57ea-8cf3-72f238d98cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094106} {:answer/id #uuid "4697884b-8a68-5b25-ae48-ac52961a3956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094107} {:answer/id #uuid "54eea33d-179b-5ebb-8bca-781adbf1b670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094108} {:answer/id #uuid "71f262c4-9cec-5233-a791-8fa255f01f1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094109} {:answer/id #uuid "7e239cc3-973d-55a9-bc44-d2fef16d3346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094110}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a3a8b73a-f5ca-5ea4-8736-6d1bbec6c71e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094105}] :question/id #uuid "5519d8f3-5f4f-5b34-b1bb-b26079a6662a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11910" :question/problem "Given that $y = \\frac{2}{3}\\ln x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6bba1a6-7ea1-5b05-9ffb-69c67a87c5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6bba1a6-7ea1-5b05-9ffb-69c67a87c5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232802} :answer-field/id #uuid "e320e47d-cc25-5e34-a058-d86a0416a0d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232801}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6a48b7a-f270-5ba0-b480-17bea4dd2da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-339941" :question/problem "Given that $y=-11\\operatorname{ln}x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-11\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =-11\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =-11\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234288 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "531eff6b-7728-5135-92da-8477ae71ccbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-70881" :question/problem "Given that $y=2\\operatorname{ln}x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237851 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e1d6f3e-9053-5690-b000-66d554fc0b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236110} {:answer/id #uuid "3532faea-48d8-5741-aa13-a64cbba7d647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{ex}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236153} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1aa2e2-8a76-5713-9b50-46a772b85443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236316} {:answer/id #uuid "a1648056-d8f0-59f6-985d-fcda1cb5175d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{e}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236828} {:answer/id #uuid "d8be5480-6829-5df9-a0e9-113723bfaa4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e1aa2e2-8a76-5713-9b50-46a772b85443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236316} :answer-field/id #uuid "994834f1-4e9a-532e-b583-a55ce29002bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237641}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "319b8cc3-c619-5308-8487-fad516398fb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-101600" :question/problem "Given that $y=2eln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2eln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5235b2d2-41a6-571c-8e01-a03aeb01451b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236336} {:answer/id #uuid "7f36f138-72b0-5be3-99c0-4538ad3f84d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236605} {:answer/id #uuid "a14212af-f2a6-570c-8589-28ef6e251469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 175